 "notes": "Libretto by Emanuel Schikaneder (1791). Words as printed in the Edition Peters vocal score, which the app follows where it differs from the libretto: \"Der, welcher wandelt\" (the libretto has \"wandert\"), \"Beschwerde\" and \"Erde\" (the libretto has \"Beschwerden\" and \"Erden\"), \"Strasse\" with ss, \"schwingt er sich von der Erde himmelan\" (the libretto has \"aus der Erde\"), \"himmel an\" in two words, \"fort zu wandeln\" in three words (the libretto has \"fortzuwandeln\"), \"schliesst\" and \"muss\" with ss, the Armed Men's \"Dir ist erlaubt\" (the libretto has \"Es ist erlaubt\"), Pamina's \"Tamino halt!\" without a comma, and the print's apostrophes (\"weih'n\", \"hör'\", \"geh'n\", \"wär'\", \"Welch'\", \"seh'n\", \"wiederseh'n\"). Repeats of the music are written out as sung: \"wenn auch der Tod beschieden wär'\" and \"ist würdig und wird eingeweiht\" twice. The two Armed Men sing the chorale in octaves on one printed staff; each has his own line here, with the same words. IPA follows sung German stage diction: final -er, -ern as [ɐ]; the prefixes er-, ver-, zer- with [ɛr]; r elsewhere rolled or flipped; ch as [ç] after front vowels and [x] after back vowels; glottal stops [ʔ] before initial vowels; final b d g devoiced.",
